---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { data } from '../lib/centres';

const { meta } = data;
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About & methodology — Irish Driving Data',
  url: `${meta.siteUrl}/about/`,
  author: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: "Liam O'Connor",
    url: `${meta.siteUrl}/about/#author`,
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Irish Driving Data',
    url: meta.siteUrl,
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & methodology | Irish Driving Data"
  description="How Irish Driving Data collects RSA Category B pass rates and waiting times from CSO statistics, how often we update, and who maintains the site."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Trust & provenance</p>
  <h1>About & methodology</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Irish Driving Data is a free tracker of Category B driving test pass rates
    and estimated waiting times for RSA test centres in Ireland. It exists so
    learners, instructors, journalists, and developers can cite current figures
    without scraping HTML.
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Data sources &amp; coverage</h2>
    <p>
      Figures come from CSO PxStat on{' '}
      <a href="https://data.cso.ie/">data.cso.ie</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://data.gov.ie">data.gov.ie</a>, published on behalf of the Road
      Safety Authority (RSA). License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>ROA30</strong> — pass rates, tests delivered, and tests not conducted /
        abandoned by centre
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>ROA36</strong> — estimated waiting time (weeks) to a driving test invite at
        month end
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This site loads the full Category B monthly series from CSO (currently January 2021
      through the latest published month). Pass rates and abandoned counts come from ROA30;
      waiting times from ROA36 (available from September 2021).
    </p>
    <p class="source-line">
      Current site snapshot: {meta.citationLong ?? meta.citation}. Data refreshed{' '}
      {meta.lastUpdated} from CSO PxStat CSV exports.
    </p>

    <h2>Comparing centres &amp; periods</h2>
    <p>On this site you can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tracker</strong> — latest month for every centre: pass rate, wait, tests delivered, no-shows, and abandoned</li>
      <li><strong>Compare</strong> — put two or three centres side by side with ranks, 12-month change, and trend charts</li>
      <li><strong>Charts</strong> — explore one centre in depth with national ranking and history charts</li>
      <li><strong>Map</strong> — interactive Ireland map with centres coloured by pass rate</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Centre pages show the full monthly history table and a pass-rate trend chart. Download
      the complete dataset as <a href="/data/latest.json">JSON</a> (includes all months per
      centre).
    </p>

    <h2>What the numbers mean</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Pass rate</strong> is the Category B pass percentage published for
      that centre in the CSO release. Where a centre has no published figure for
      the month, we show “Not published” — we do not invent values.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Waiting time</strong> is the CSO’s estimated weeks to a test invite
      at month end. It is <em>not</em> a live feed of MyRoadSafety appointment
      slots. Always confirm booking availability on the RSA / MyRoadSafety
      service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Tests delivered</strong> is the count of Category B driving tests
      conducted that month (ROA30). <strong>No-shows</strong> are candidates who
      did not attend their booked test. <strong>Abandoned</strong> tests are those
      not conducted / abandoned before completion (ROA30).
    </p>

    <h2>Update cadence</h2>
    <p>
      CSO publishes driving-test statistics monthly. Re-run{' '}
      <code>npm run data</code> to fetch the latest CSO CSVs and rebuild the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Reuse & citation</h2>
    <p>
      Download the same dataset as
      <a href="/data/latest.csv">CSV</a> or
      <a href="/data/latest.json">JSON</a>. Embed a compact centre card with our
      <a href="/embed-demo/">embed snippet</a>. Please credit Irish Driving Data
      and the underlying CSO / RSA sources.
    </p>

    <h2 id="author">Who maintains this</h2>
    <p>
      Written and maintained by <strong>Liam O'Connor</strong>. The project is
      maintained by <a href="https://www.driveflow.ie">DriveFlow</a>, which also
      publishes Google Maps practice routes for RSA centres. Irish Driving Data
      is a separate, free resource — it is not a substitute for official RSA
      advice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions or corrections:
      <a href="mailto:driveflowweb@gmail.com">driveflowweb@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
